            <div xml:id="d829">

                <pb facs="0929" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/666: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-10T19:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 10, 1919,
                                7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department informed that Federico Tinoco of Costa Rica is sending Francisco
                    Farron and Maraino Zungigab [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] to Guatemala by
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">City of Para</hi> or steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Izabal</hi> in hope of obtaining arms and
                    ammunition.</p>
                <p>Tactfully point out to Guatemalan Government Department’s attitude toward Tinoco
                    as well as the position assumed in the Washington convention expressing hope
                    that Guatemala will continue as ever faithful to the spirit therein set
                    forth.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
